// @run
// @log 3
// @log 4
// D1598 — TWO SIBLING TOP-LEVEL BLOCKS BINDING ONE NAME MADE THE HOLE PARAMETER'S PIN
// DECLINE, EVEN WHEN BOTH BINDINGS HAD THE SAME TYPE. `moduleLocalLetOfUnique` answers -1 on
// any duplicated name because the table behind it is first-wins over a walk with no notion of
// which block a call site sits in (D1596). Where the candidates DISAGREE that decline is the
// safe answer; here they are both `{base: i32}`, so every candidate pins the same rep and the
// decline cost a working program: the instance took the `"i32"` catch-all over a `(ref $type)`
// argument.
//
// Renaming either binding ran. One block ran. Both blocks inside a FUNCTION ran — the module
// frame is the only scope whose block bindings had no lexical resolution here.
//
// The UFCS spelling of the same call was the CLAUSE-1 face, check-clean invalid wasm:
// `scripts/capability-probes/hole-param-sibling-blocks-of-one-type.vl`. The single-file
// spelling is `tests/cases/generics/pin-sibling-block-bindings.vl` — the module boundary is
// not an ingredient, which is what makes this a module-frame table defect.
import { hbase } from "./cell"

if true {
  const n = { base: 3 }
  print(n.base)
}

if true {
  const n = { base: 4 }
  print(hbase(n))
}
